# 10 — Backend / PostgreSQL

- PostgreSQL only. Do not introduce SQLite, MySQL, or other primary stores.
- Use typed SQLAlchemy 2.x models with `DeclarativeBase` metadata from `app.db.base`.
- All schema changes go through Alembic migrations. Keep a single migration head.
- Prefer explicit transactions; commit only after successful unit-of-work completion.
- Design write paths for idempotency where retries are expected.
- Enforce permission checks at the API/service boundary before mutating state.
- No direct write access to the ERP V2 database. Integration must be API/contract based.
- Never request or use ERP V2 production credentials.
- Keep development and test databases distinct from any V2 instance.
